<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Sporta — the sitemap index.

  THE PRODUCT ENTRY CARRIES NO lastmod, ON PURPOSE.

  It used to say 2026-07-26, stamped when this file was built. But
  sitemap-products.xml is not a file any more: .htaccess rewrites it to
  api/sitemap-products.php, which generates it from the catalogue in MySQL and
  stamps its own lastmod from the data — 2026-08-22 when this was written, a
  month later than the number here claimed.

  lastmod in an INDEX is the one signal a crawler uses to decide whether a
  child sitemap is worth re-fetching. A value that is permanently older than
  the sitemap it describes says "nothing has changed here" every time the
  catalogue changes, which is the exact opposite of what it is for. A product
  added in /backends would sit uncrawled behind a date from before it existed.

  Omitting it is valid — the sitemaps protocol makes lastmod optional — and it
  means the crawler falls back to its own schedule instead of trusting a stamp
  that cannot be right. A correct value would have to be generated, and this
  file is static; making it dynamic to carry one number is a bigger change than
  the number is worth, and the sitemap it points at already stamps itself
  correctly.

  The pages entry keeps its lastmod because that one IS a static file, built at
  the same time as this, so the date is true for as long as both are.
-->
<sitemapindex xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
  <sitemap>
    <loc>https://www.sporta.com.kw/sitemap-pages.xml</loc>
    <lastmod>2026-08-20T11:00:52.012Z</lastmod>
  </sitemap>
  <sitemap>
    <loc>https://www.sporta.com.kw/sitemap-products.xml</loc>
  </sitemap>
</sitemapindex>
